body:
With the schema now unconditionally `$defs/uint64`, RV32 configurations can supply values larger than 32 bits because there is no `MXLEN == 32 -> ARCH_ID_VALUE <= 32'hffffffff` (or equivalent) requirement. Previously the RV32 schema enforced the width via `$defs/uint32`; consider adding an explicit RV32 upper-bound requirement so `marchid`-sized values remain representable on RV32.
```suggestion
    MXLEN == 32 -> ARCH_ID_VALUE != 32'h80000000;
    MXLEN == 32 -> ARCH_ID_VALUE <= 32'hffffffff;
```
